  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">FSL, WASH and protection for conflict-affected communties in Syria and Gaza - EH</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project supports crisis -affected women, men, girls, and boys with life -saving humanitarian aid by improving access to safe, equitable Water Sanitation and Hygiene (WASH), protection, and food security services. It ensures dignified access to safe water, gender -sensitive sanitation, and hygiene materials. Protection efforts help communities safeguard their rights and reduce risks of abuse. Food -insecure individuals receive emergency assistance through cash or food aid. Additionally, the project promotes women&apos;s leadership in humanitarian response by identifying barriers and enablers to their engagement and offering regional recommendations (Occupied Palestinian Territories (OPT), Syria).</narrative>
  </description>
